z2j = z2h (u6x + CASH under the exact ledger) + CASH_END 1880: an endgame trigger for the same rescue formation.
From round 1880 a lone king's babies run CASH's group, site, squeak and promote (no raw cheese needed; the leader is
the heaviest, then the lowest ID, of 3+ babies within 4, 5+ from the king), while the bank keeps a new king alive to
round 2000: bank >= max(60, 4 * (2000 - round - 55) + 10) (two kings eat 4 a round; a starving king loses 10 health a
round and a new one has up to 600, so it outlives 55 rounds on an empty bank). Kings formed before 1200 count, and the
engine allows only 2 after it, so the trigger is exactly "one king left".
Why: at r2000 the war points are cat damage 0.3, kings 0.5, transfer 0.2 of 100, each split by share (GameWorld.
setWinnerIfMorePoints); 1 king to their 1 is 25-25 and 2 to 1 is 33-17. u6x's END_KING (from r1850) needs 400 banked
and the king itself to name a site; 9 of the 12 lone-king replica points losses never had 400, and z1g's dynamic bar
failed on mechanics (no site, a king lost after forming). CASH's formation is baby-led and formed in 7 of 8 chain games
(cq2). zc6's own cells: u6x lost araid evileye A 49-50 with kings 1-1 and 576 banked; won wallsofparadis B,
learn_your_lesson A and B 1-1 on kings.
The ledger keeps every game in which neither trigger fires identical to u6x's (z2h's validation applies: the change is
inside cashTick, which runs in z2h's measured hook).
